   258|- [ ] The issue-body `3 real plans` requirement is satisfied by the existence + minimum-bar validation of #2045/#2046/#2047 for the four providers named in the issue body at planning time; additional exemplar drift beyond that minimum bar becomes follow-up work on the owning issues rather than #2045 rewrite scope.
   259|---
   260|
   261|## Adversarial Review Summary
   262|
   263|| Date | Provider | Verdict | Status |
   264||---|---|---|---|
   265|| 2026-04-15 | Codex | MAJOR | Current blocker state is tracked by the latest dedicated rereview artifact listed below; older Codex waves are historical context only |
   266|| 2026-04-15 | Gemini | MAJOR | Historical baseline review; current-text refresh attempts are currently capacity-blocked |
   267|| 2026-04-15 | Claude | MINOR | Historical current-text refresh attempts are unreliable; use latest successful artifact as context only |
   268|
   269|Full review artifacts: `scripts/review/results/2026-04-14-plan-2045-codex.md`, `scripts/review/results/2026-04-14-plan-2045-gemini.md`, `scripts/review/results/2026-04-15-plan-2045-claude.md`, `scripts/review/results/2026-04-15-plan-2045-codex-rereview22.md`
   270|
   271|**Current status:** Not approval-ready. Fresh re-review is still required after each substantive revision until the newest authoritative provider artifact set reduces blockers to MINOR/APPROVE for the current revision.
   272|
   273|---
   274|
   275|## Risks and Open Questions
   276|
   277|- **Risk:** “all agents” scope creep — a new provider added after #2045 closes will require follow-up onboarding work rather than reopening this issue. Mitigation: the table freezes scope to the providers named in the issue body at planning time.
   278|- **Risk:** example plans (#2046, #2047) may drift from the template after #2045 closes. Mitigation: `test_issue_2045_example_plans.sh` can be rerun as a regression check; semantic drift there becomes follow-up work on the owning issues.
   279|- **Risk:** provider onboarding can still drift if one adapter only references canonical shared docs while another embeds the workflow directly. Mitigation: `test_issue_2045_onboarding_docs.sh` and `test_issue_2045_policy_alignment.sh` use explicit per-file pass criteria and reject deprecated workflow routes.
   280|- **Risk:** `.codex/CODEX.md` and `.claude/skills/coordination/issue-planning-mode/SKILL.md` contain legacy/structural drift beyond simple gate-order wording. Mitigation: both are now in implementation scope or explicit skill-alignment coverage.
   281|- **Resolved:** false safe-path blocker claim — corrected in resource intelligence; `test_issue_2045_safe_path_assumption.sh` prevents regression.
   282|- **Resolved:** missing Claude review artifact — `scripts/review/results/2026-04-15-plan-2045-claude.md` now exists and is included in the three-provider review set.
   283|
   284|---
   285|
   286|## Complexity: T2
   287|
   288|**T2** — multi-surface governance/onboarding alignment across docs, skills, and example-plan validation.
   289|
```
